## STANDING LINES
1. **PRIOR-WORK CHECK, before you edit (a READY without a PRIOR WORK section is returned unread).** On `885692995df9`: `git log --oneline -n 8 -- web/e2e/journey.spec.ts` and `-- web/e2e/journey.ts` and `-- web/playwright.config.ts` (name them); `git grep -n -E 'warm|HPSMPOC-110' 885692995df9 -- web/e2e web/src/server/warmup-render.ts web/playwright.config.ts` (name every hit: another warm-up changes the fix); `git grep -n 'journey.spec\|walkJourney' 885692995df9 -- web/e2e web/scripts` (who shares the walk; positive control: `journey.ts` is a hit). State what you reuse (`walkJourney`, `Span`, `warmUpMs`, the `TIMED` project split) and what you add. Jira: none needed (no write, no read required).
2. **CodeQL.** Push the one ref only, plainly, never force; read it back with `ls-remote`; a CodeQL alert is FIXED IN THE CODE, never dismissed, no ruleset bypass asked for. Tuesday lands (head-pinned squash, per the landing precedent above); it is Tuesday's, not yours.
3. **PHASE SCOPE.** This phase builds no integration with HP tools (Security Manager API, Fleet Threat Assessment, firmware tools, SIEM). Next-phase items are stored and architected only, never built, and never shown to HP as done. If a ticket needs one, STOP and ask Tuesday.
4. **No production, no demo deploy, no hosted site, no HTTP to any hosted host, no `az`, no Kudu, no docker, no App Service setting.** The only network is `npm ci`, a missing-browser `npx playwright install chromium`, `git push`/`git fetch`, `gh` GETs, and your own loopback servers in your block (stop every one you start; record the ports free again). Nothing deploys.
5. **No message to any human.** No mail, chat or PR comment; you never open, merge, edit or comment on a PR and never write Jira. No person's name in STATUS, code, test titles or commit messages (say "the product owner"). No decision-card id and no `C-` entry number in changed lines; no `B###` id in a commit message or test text. Client names: Datasec/HPSM-POC only. No Artifact, Docs, publish, decision-queue or scoreboard tool.
6. **WORDS.** No customer-visible string changes in this lane. All added text is ASCII.
7. **Never skip a failure.** A failing test, lint, build, e2e row or CI job: fix the root cause and re-verify end to end; never `skip`, `only`, `fixme`, retry, sleep-for-timing or environment-gate; never loosen a budget (see Step 5). **Never delete** (`rm`, `git branch -d/-D`, `--prune`, `update-ref -d`, `worktree prune`, `gc`, `reset`, `clean`, `stash`); quarantine to `.tools/b905/_quarantine/`. Never rebase, never amend, never force-push. A mutant file is restored by `cp` from the committed blob.
8. **Shell:** never type `cd` (a hook refuses it); absolute single-quoted paths (they contain `!`); `git -C`; `/usr/bin/grep -i` with a positive control for every count; write `${VAR}:path`; no unquoted word starting with `=`; heredocs QUOTED; `python3 -I` only. **Every count printed in STATUS is printed by the command that makes it.** Kill a process only by pid plus cwd. Never wait with `pgrep -f <pattern>` from a shell whose own argv holds the pattern.
